  "_comment": "The native lane, lane 1: every exchange in order, as any App server must answer it. Requests: {{name}} is a value an earlier step saved. Response bodies match exactly, except strings of the form <kind>: <device_bearer> sewdv_ and 43 base64url, <code> 43 base64url, <session_id> 22 base64url, <timestamp> an ISO 8601 time, <media_url> a wss:// URL, <app_url> an https:// URL, <door_code> the host door's one-time code (k2lgn_ and base64url), <any> anything. A step with \"to\": \"host\" is the native client's own request to the host's sign-in door (K2's /.k2/auth/* on the App's address), not to the lane. Headers listed must be present with that value. The people and channels are the test's: bob signs in with his password; channel 5 is a voice channel, 6 a DM; recording 77 (channel 7, started by alice, 1001) asks for consent: the 409's detail is Sew's own error.details (reason, the recording as bob sees it, auto, consent_prompt) and the consent's 200 is Sew's recording as bob sees it after his answer. Record and Stop (voice/recording) pass Sew's answers unchanged: bob starts recording 79 in channel 5 and stops it; recording 77's room requires its recording while two or more are in it, so its stop is Sew's 422 recording_required. Last, bob signs in on a second install through the host's sign-in door: the lane begins (an id and a PKCE challenge; the verifier stays on the server), the client posts his password with the challenge to the host's door, and the lane trades the door's code for a device session.",
